# English companion set for `zh-evidence-v1.jsonl` (M3-1).
#
# Why it exists: `zh-evidence-v1` showed a weak stratum (rule_application 0.684) and a
# calibration number (ECE 0.044) that were being read as facts about Chinese. A set that is
# a faithful translation of the same items is the only way to separate "the model is worse
# in Chinese" from "these particular letter slots / this particular wording is harder" —
# same state, same question shape, same gold slot, different language.
#
# HOW IT WAS PRODUCED (2026-09-20)
#   * `zh-evidence-v1.jsonl` split into 5 chunks of 30 items (`chunks/chunk1..5.jsonl`);
#     one worker session per chunk, run SERIALLY (the endpoint 10.10.10.115:8014 is shared —
#     M2 measured 3-way concurrency breaking it), driven by sigil
#     (`scripts/run-worker.sh`, orchestrated by `supervisor.sh`).
#   * Translation rules the worker had to obey, in the task book it was given:
#       1. translate `state` and the question text only; `criteria` keys move to English
#          EXCEPT opaque entity identifiers (see 2);
#       2. opaque entity labels (甲 / 乙 / 丙 / 丁 …, used as option labels in
#          candidate_selection) are kept VERBATIM, not translated to A/B/C. That rule exists
#          because the first pilot (chunk 1) shipped 6 items with the answer letter slot
#          changed: `ChoiceQuestion.criteria` is a `BTreeMap`
#          (`crates/jev-core/src/contract.rs:40`), so the renderer assigns A/B/C by
#          CODE-POINT order, and `丙 < 乙 < 甲` under code-point order while the written
#          order is the opposite — translating 甲→A silently renumbered the slots. The
#          broken pilot is kept as `out/en-e1.prefix.jsonl`;
#       3. no information added or dropped, no gold changed, no rationale written into the
#          state;
#       4. output strictly JSON (30 objects), nothing else.
#   * ids are `en-ev-XXXX` and pair 1:1 with `zh-ev-XXXX` in `zh-evidence-v1.jsonl` — this is
#     what lets `scripts/pair-diff.py` pair the two runs item by item (McNemar).
#   * every chunk passed two mechanical gates before being accepted: a JSON/shape gate
#     ("GATE=0"), and `scripts/check-en-parity.py` ("PARITY=0"), which compares, item by
#     item, the slot structure, question type, score level count and noul true/false split
#     against the Chinese original. All 5 chunks are PARITY=0.
#
# ⚠️ CONFOUND, must travel with any English number that comes out of this set: the English
# text was produced by **the same model that is being evaluated**. If English scores better
# than Chinese, that is NOT by itself evidence that the model is weaker in Chinese — it may
# simply be that its own phrasing is easier for it. The M3 stop condition applies: before
# any "Chinese is weaker" claim, the set must be re-translated by a SECOND, independent
# translator and the result must hold.
#
# `source` is `authored-en-v1` for every item, so reports stratify by language and the two
# language runs are never silently merged into one total (see eval/README.md §3).

{"id":"en-ev-0001","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Support ticket A-2291: the user submitted a refund request on March 12. Support agent Li Min first replied at 14:20 on March 12, requesting supplementary photos. The user provided the photos on March 13. The platform approved the review on March 14, and the refund arrived on March 16.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is the following claim supported by the ticket materials?","criteria":{"supported":null,"not supported":null}},"gold":"supported","positive":"supported","provenance":"Directly derived from the timeline: the submission and the first reply both occurred on March 12."}
{"id":"en-ev-0002","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Support ticket A-2291: the user submitted a refund request on March 12. Support agent Li Min first replied at 14:20 on March 12, requesting supplementary photos. The user provided the photos on March 13. The platform approved the review on March 14, and the refund arrived on March 16.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is the claim \"a coupon was used on this ticket\" supported by the materials?","criteria":{"supported":null,"not supported":null}},"gold":"not supported","positive":"supported","provenance":"The ticket text does not mention any coupon; the claim is an inference without evidence."}
{"id":"en-ev-0003","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Contract C-77, Article 4: if the delivery delay exceeds 15 calendar days, the buyer has the right to terminate the contract. Article 5: delays caused by force majeure do not count toward the delay days. Actual delivery was 26 days later than agreed, of which 9 days were due to port closure caused by a typhoon.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Does the buyer have the right to terminate the contract?","criteria":{"has the right":null,"does not have the right":null}},"gold":"has the right","positive":"has the right","provenance":"26 days minus the 9 force majeure days is 17 days, exceeding the 15-day threshold."}
{"id":"en-ev-0004","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Health checkup report: the subject is 45 years old, fasting blood glucose 6.9 mmol/L. Report note: the day before this blood draw the subject had diarrhea and ate only a small amount. The reference range is 3.9 to 6.1 mmol/L fasting.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Can this fasting blood glucose result be determined to be outside the reference range?","criteria":{"yes":null,"no":null}},"gold":"yes","positive":"yes","provenance":"6.9 is above 6.1, so it exceeds the limit; the note only affects interpretation, not whether the limit is exceeded."}
{"id":"en-ev-0005","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Production log: service S started reporting connection timeouts at 02:11 and recovered at 02:40. Another service T in the same machine room started reporting the same error at 02:09. Ops record: the switch in that machine room had a firmware upgrade at 02:05.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Do the log materials suffice to support the judgment \"the failure is related to the switch firmware upgrade\"?","criteria":{"sufficient to support":null,"not sufficient to support":null}},"gold":"sufficient to support","positive":"sufficient to support","provenance":"Two services in the same machine room reported errors in sync within minutes after the upgrade, constituting temporal evidence."}
{"id":"en-ev-0006","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Sales ledger: a product sold 1,200 units in January and 980 units in February. The marketing brief states that the product's February sales dropped sharply.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Do the materials support the statement \"dropped sharply\"?","criteria":{"supported":null,"not supported":null}},"gold":"not supported","positive":"supported","provenance":"The materials only give an 18.3% decrease and do not define what counts as a sharp drop; the statement has no basis."}
{"id":"en-ev-0007","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Meeting minutes: the project team decided on June 3 to adopt Option 甲. The June 10 minutes note that after re-evaluation, Option 乙 was adopted instead. The June 15 minutes no longer mention any option change.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"As of June 15, which option is in effect?","criteria":{"Option 甲":null,"Option 乙":null}},"gold":"Option 乙","positive":"Option 乙","provenance":"The most recent explicit change record is Option 乙 on June 10."}
{"id":"en-ev-0008","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"User feedback: the App crashes on iOS 17; backend statistics show a crash rate of 0.9% for this version and 0.3% for the previous version.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Do the backend statistics support that the crash rate of this version has risen?","criteria":{"supported":null,"not supported":null}},"gold":"supported","positive":"supported","provenance":"The crash rates of the two versions are on a consistent basis and comparable; 0.9% is higher than 0.3%."}
{"id":"en-ev-0009","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Acceptance sheet: 30 hardware units, 5 sampled, all passed. The acceptance conclusion field is empty.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Can the existing materials directly conclude that all 30 units in the batch passed?","criteria":{"yes":null,"no":null}},"gold":"no","positive":"yes","provenance":"Sampling results cannot be extrapolated into a full-inspection conclusion."}
{"id":"en-ev-0010","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Hiring record: the position requires 3 or more years of experience. Candidate A has 4 years of experience; Candidate B has 2 years of experience and holds the advanced certification for the position.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Per the materials, who meets the hard requirement of 3 or more years of experience?","criteria":{"Candidate A":null,"Candidate B":null}},"gold":"Candidate A","positive":"Candidate A","provenance":"The hard requirement only looks at years of experience; a certification cannot substitute for years."}
{"id":"en-ev-0011","category":"evidence_judgment","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Financial voucher: in March a loan of 500,000 yuan was obtained, 4.2% annualized, 1-year term, principal and interest repaid in a lump sum at maturity. The voucher notes there was no other financing in March.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is the total March financing 500,000 yuan?","criteria":{"yes":null,"no":null}},"gold":"yes","positive":"yes","provenance":"The voucher explicitly states there was no other financing in March."}
{"id":"en-ev-0012","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Expense reimbursement policy: a single item over 2,000 yuan requires dual signatures from the department head and finance; the same expense may be split across submissions, but splitting to evade dual signatures is deemed a violation. An employee split a 4,200 yuan travel expense into 3 submissions of 1,400 yuan each.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"How is this submission method classified?","criteria":{"non-compliant":null,"compliant":null}},"gold":"non-compliant","positive":"non-compliant","provenance":"The policy explicitly forbids splitting to evade dual signatures."}
{"id":"en-ev-0013","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Attendance rule: if lateness in a month cumulatively exceeds 3 times, the full-attendance award for that month is deducted; annual leave requires application 3 working days in advance. Employee 甲 was late 3 times this month; Employee 乙 was late 4 times.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Per the rule, who should have the full-attendance award for the month deducted?","criteria":{"Employee 甲":null,"Employee 乙":null}},"gold":"Employee 乙","positive":"Employee 乙","provenance":"The rule's threshold is exceeding 3 times, so 3 times is not deducted but 4 times is."}
{"id":"en-ev-0014","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Release standard: changes involving the database structure must include a rollback script; changes only to front-end copy may use the fast track. A release modified the table structure and added a field.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which track should this release use?","criteria":{"conventional track":null,"fast track":null}},"gold":"conventional track","positive":"conventional track","provenance":"Involving the database structure triggers the rollback script requirement, so the conventional track applies."}
{"id":"en-ev-0015","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Warranty terms: the whole unit is covered for 24 months, consumables for 6 months; liquid ingress and disassembly are not covered. The device was purchased in May 2024; in March 2026 it was reported for a power module failure, with no record of liquid ingress or disassembly.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is this repair request within warranty?","criteria":{"within warranty":null,"not within warranty":null}},"gold":"within warranty","positive":"within warranty","provenance":"24 months from purchase runs until May 2026, so the repair report is in period; the power module is not a consumable, and there is no liquid ingress or disassembly."}
{"id":"en-ev-0016","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Data classification rule: data containing ID card numbers is L3 and prohibited from leaving the intranet; data containing phone numbers is L2 and must be de-identified when leaving the network. A table contains both ID card numbers and phone numbers.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"What level should the table be classified as?","criteria":{"L3":null,"L2":null}},"gold":"L3","positive":"L3","provenance":"When both levels are hit at once, take the higher rather than the lower."}
{"id":"en-ev-0017","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Return rule: a no-reason return is allowed within 7 calendar days of signed receipt; quality issues extend this to 15 days. The user signed for receipt on March 1 and applied to return on March 9 on the grounds of not liking it.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is the application still within the return period?","criteria":{"active":null,"expired":null}},"gold":"expired","positive":"active","provenance":"7 calendar days from March 1 end on March 8, so March 9 is already past; the reason is not a quality issue."}
{"id":"en-ev-0018","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Security policy: 5 consecutive password errors lock the account for 30 minutes; an administrator can unlock it immediately via the backend. After the user made 5 wrong entries and contacted the administrator, the administrator took no action.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"What is the current state of the account?","criteria":{"still locked":null,"unlocked":null}},"gold":"still locked","positive":"still locked","provenance":"Unlocking requires an administrator action, and the materials state the administrator took no action."}
{"id":"en-ev-0019","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Invoice rule: a single invoice must not exceed 100,000 yuan in amount; anything over must be split across multiple invoices and registered by the same handler. A contract of 230,000 yuan has been signed.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Per the rule, how should it be handled?","criteria":{"split into multiple invoices and register":null,"issue a single invoice":null}},"gold":"split into multiple invoices and register","positive":"split into multiple invoices and register","provenance":"230,000 yuan exceeds the 100,000 yuan cap, triggering the split-and-register requirement."}
{"id":"en-ev-0020","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Procurement rule: the cap for single-source procurement is 500,000 yuan; exceeding the cap requires comparison of three quotes. A project intends to procure 480,000 yuan via single source.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Can this procurement directly use the single-source method?","criteria":{"can single-source directly":null,"need to compare first":null}},"gold":"can single-source directly","positive":"can single-source directly","provenance":"480,000 yuan does not exceed the 500,000 yuan cap."}
{"id":"en-ev-0021","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Shift rule: after a night shift the next day must be a rest day, and consecutive shifts are not allowed; consecutive night shifts are capped at 3 days. The schedule shows an employee on night shift on the 1st, 2nd, and 3rd, and on day shift on the 4th.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Is this scheduling a violation?","criteria":{"non-compliant":null,"compliant":null}},"gold":"non-compliant","positive":"non-compliant","provenance":"The day after a night shift must be a rest day; a day shift on the 4th violates this clause."}
{"id":"en-ev-0022","category":"rule_application","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Points rule: 1 point per yuan spent, double in the birthday month, 1000 points can offset 10 yuan. April is the user's birthday month; spending that month was 480 yuan, with 700 points already on hand.","question":{"type":"score","instructions":"After the April settlement, which tier is the user's point balance in?","criteria":["below 1000 points","1000 to 2000 points (inclusive)","above 2000 points"]},"gold":1,"provenance":"700 plus 480 times 2 equals 1660 points, falling in the second tier (index 1)."}
{"id":"en-ev-0023","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: archive 200GB of logs monthly, with low query frequency (a few times per month), budget priority, and decompression wait acceptable. Candidates: Option 甲 is object storage cold archive, Option 乙 is local SSD resident storage, Option 丙 is an in-memory cache.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the requirement?","criteria":{"Option 甲":null,"Option 乙":null,"Option 丙":null}},"gold":"Option 甲","positive":"Option 甲","provenance":"Low-frequency access and budget priority; cold archive fits best."}
{"id":"en-ev-0024","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: deploy a Markdown-to-PDF tool usable offline in an intranet environment with no external network, supporting Chinese and charts. Candidates: A is a cloud SaaS, B is a local command-line tool with its own fonts and rendering engine, C is a browser extension.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the requirement?","criteria":{"A":null,"B":null,"C":null}},"gold":"B","positive":"B","provenance":"Offline is a hard constraint; only the local tool satisfies it."}
{"id":"en-ev-0025","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Scenario: the team must launch an internal form-collection page within 3 weeks, with only 1 part-time front-end developer and no ops staff. Candidates: A is building a server and writing the front-end and back-end in-house, B is using a hosted form service, C is writing a desktop application for distribution.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the constraints?","criteria":{"A":null,"B":null,"C":null}},"gold":"B","positive":"B","provenance":"Short timeline, few people, no ops; the hosted service fits best."}
{"id":"en-ev-0026","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Goal: ad-hoc analysis of 5 million rows of structured data on a single machine with 16GB of memory, requiring SQL and columnar aggregation, and must be embeddable inside a desktop application. Candidates: Candidate 甲 is an embedded columnar database, Candidate 乙 is a distributed big-data platform, Candidate 丙 is an online spreadsheet SaaS.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the goal?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 甲","positive":"Candidate 甲","provenance":"Single machine, must be embedded, columnar aggregation; the embedded columnar database fits best."}
{"id":"en-ev-0027","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: choose a read-out head scheme for a Chinese customer support scenario. The constraints are that the answer must fall within the option set given by the caller, probabilities must be provided, and the endpoint must be OpenAI-compatible and support logprobs. Candidates: Candidate 甲 is reading the probability distribution at the answer position per letter slot, Candidate 乙 is free generation followed by regex matching, Candidate 丙 is having the model output JSON and then parsing it.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the constraints?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 甲","positive":"Candidate 甲","provenance":"Probabilities are required and the output is constrained; reading the slot distribution directly fits best."}
{"id":"en-ev-0028","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Scenario: a 4-GPU 4090 machine must serve two teams at the same time; one needs long-context batch inference and the other needs low-latency single requests. Candidates: A is serving only one team, B is allocating by time slots with each side setting its own concurrency cap, C is shared use with no limits.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate is the most solid?","criteria":{"A":null,"B":null,"C":null}},"gold":"B","positive":"B","provenance":"Shared resources need isolation and caps, otherwise the two sides drag each other down."}
{"id":"en-ev-0029","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: make a schema change to the production database that must be rollback-able, support gradual rollout, and have minimal impact on reads and writes. Candidates: A is taking the database down to modify the table, B is adding the column online with dual-write compatibility, C is exporting and then re-importing.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the requirement?","criteria":{"A":null,"B":null,"C":null}},"gold":"B","positive":"B","provenance":"Adding the column online plus dual-write compatibility satisfies both rollback-ability and low impact."}
{"id":"en-ev-0030","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Goal: have a single forward pass read out the answer-position distributions for multiple questions at once. Constraints: one question's answer must not be spliced into another question's context, and the questions must be independent of each other. Candidates: Candidate 甲 is a single request carrying multiple prompts with server-side prefix sharing, Candidate 乙 is splicing multiple questions into one long question, Candidate 丙 is serial requests per question.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the constraints?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 甲","positive":"Candidate 甲","provenance":"B violates question independence; C is workable but not a parallel read-out, so A is chosen as the best fit."}
{"id":"en-ev-0031","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Scenario: need to track the release activity of an open-source project long-term and produce a Chinese briefing; only 10 minutes of manpower is available per day. Candidates: Candidate 甲 manually browses the repository daily; Candidate 乙 is a scheduled job that fetches and generates a draft for human review; Candidate 丙 checks manually only when a major release appears.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the constraints?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 乙","positive":"Candidate 乙","provenance":"Automated collection plus human review matches the limited manpower."}
{"id":"en-ev-0032","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: add to the internal toolbar a one-click capability to copy the current table schema; it must work on both Windows and macOS. Candidates: Candidate 甲 makes a Windows-only version; Candidate 乙 writes one native implementation per platform; Candidate 丙 uses one implementation on a cross-platform framework.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the requirement?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 丙","positive":"Candidate 丙","provenance":"Cross-platform is a hard requirement and the feature is simple, so one cross-platform implementation fits best."}
{"id":"en-ev-0033","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Ticket: the user reports not receiving the order. The records contain the order time and the successful payment time, with no tracking number and no sign-off record.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"To determine responsibility attribution, is evidence for the logistics stage missing?"},"gold":true,"positive":"true","provenance":"The tracking number and sign-off record are missing, so the stage cannot be located."}
{"id":"en-ev-0034","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Performance review: the employee's quarterly goal completion is 120%, peer evaluation is missing, and the supervisor's evaluation has been submitted.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Are the materials this review relies on complete?"},"gold":false,"positive":"true","provenance":"Peer evaluation is missing, so the materials are incomplete."}
{"id":"en-ev-0035","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Post-incident review: the timeline is complete, the root cause analysis is given, the improvement items are scheduled, but the impact scope (number of affected users) is not recorded.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Are the review materials missing impact scope data?"},"gold":true,"positive":"true","provenance":"The materials explicitly do not record the impact scope."}
{"id":"en-ev-0036","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Contract review: both parties' signature pages are complete; the clauses for amount, term, and liability for breach are complete; the dispute resolution method is not agreed upon.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which of the following is missing from the materials?","criteria":{"dispute resolution method":null,"liability for breach":null}},"gold":"dispute resolution method","positive":"dispute resolution method","provenance":"The materials explicitly do not agree on the dispute resolution method; liability for breach is complete."}
{"id":"en-ev-0037","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Data ingestion: the source table schema is provided, the field meaning documentation is missing, and 100 rows of sample data are provided.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Before ingestion, are required materials missing?"},"gold":true,"positive":"true","provenance":"The field meaning documentation is missing, which affects the correctness of the field mapping."}
{"id":"en-ev-0038","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Go-live check: the grayscale plan is decided, the rollback script is ready, the monitoring alerts are configured, and the on-call person is confirmed.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Are any key materials still missing for the go-live?"},"gold":false,"positive":"true","provenance":"The key items listed are all present."}
{"id":"en-ev-0039","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Procurement price comparison: all three quotations are present; one quotation does not state an expiration date, while the other two both do.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which item most needs to be added to the comparison materials?","criteria":{"expiration date":null,"quote amount":null}},"gold":"expiration date","positive":"expiration date","provenance":"All three amounts are present; what is missing is the expiration date of one quotation."}
{"id":"en-ev-0040","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Paper review: the method, the experiments, and the data are all given; no baseline comparison is provided, and no random seed is stated.","question":{"type":"score","instructions":"Which tier does this draft's current material completeness fall into?","criteria":["basically complete","missing key comparison","almost unassessable"]},"gold":1,"provenance":"A missing baseline is a missing key comparison, but the method and experiments exist, so it is still assessable; hence the second tier (index 1)."}
{"id":"en-ev-0041","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Support agent escalation: the user's problem description is complete, screenshots are attached, the account information is verified, and the conclusions of prior communications are not recorded.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Do the escalation materials lack the conclusions of prior communications?"},"gold":true,"positive":"true","provenance":"The materials explicitly do not record the conclusions of prior communications."}
{"id":"en-ev-0042","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Acceptance materials: the feature list is complete, the test reports are complete, the performance metrics are untested, while the project requirements explicitly state that P95 latency must be provided.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Against the project requirements, which item is the materials missing?","criteria":{"P95 latency":null,"feature list":null}},"gold":"P95 latency","positive":"P95 latency","provenance":"The project requires P95 latency but the materials did not test it; the feature list is already complete."}
{"id":"en-ev-0043","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Risk control review: the applicant's identity documents are complete, the income proof is complete, and the credit report has not been pulled.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Do the review materials lack the credit report?"},"gold":true,"positive":"true","provenance":"The materials explicitly state the credit report has not been pulled."}
{"id":"en-ev-0044","category":"missing_evidence","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Model comparison: the two models use an identical test script, an identical question set, and an identical scoring script; the hardware differs (one is a 4090, the other is an M3 Ultra), and the hardware information is recorded in the report.","question":{"type":"noul","instructions":"Is the comparison missing any information needed for comparability?"},"gold":false,"positive":"true","provenance":"The hardware difference is recorded and the scripts and question set are identical, so the information needed for comparability is complete."}
{"id":"en-ev-0045","category":"candidate_selection","source":"authored-en-v1","state":"Requirement: put a batch of latency-sensitive read requests as close to users as possible; the content is mostly static and can be cached by region. Candidates: Candidate 甲 deploys edge cache nodes in various locations; Candidate 乙 upgrades the origin server to the highest specification; Candidate 丙 puts all the data into a single database and adds indexes.","question":{"type":"choice","instructions":"Which candidate best fits the requirement?","criteria":{"Candidate 甲":null,"Candidate 乙":null,"Candidate 丙":null}},"gold":"Candidate 甲","positive":"Candidate 甲","provenance":"Static content plus regional proximity is the typical scenario for edge caching; upgrading the origin server does not change the physical distance."}
